incident :the_liangzhou_double_return do
  name "The Liangzhou Double Return"
  tags :governance, :identity, :legitimacy, :legibility
  prominence :recognized

  prose <<~PROSE
    Two admitted pieces at the #{ref :juyan_register_house, "Juyan Register House"}, read four years apart, both giving the 2061 household register of a Liangzhou ward and disagreeing about forty-one households. The first arrived in 2082 and the second in 2086, from two different copying houses over the same road.

    The sheets agree on eleven hundred and eighty-two households, on the ward boundary and on the collection year. On the forty-one they do not: one return enters them in the ward, the other omits them. Neither reading can be taken again, because #{ref :the_squeeze, "each sheet consumed the face that gave it"}, and no third copy has come in. Under #{ref :entry_into_the_register, "the register's procedure"} both returns stand admitted and the conflict is entered as its own numbered item, open in #{year :now} CE.
  PROSE

  prose <<~PROSE, section: :aftermath, heading: "The Eleven Households"
    Eleven households at #{ref :juyan, "Juyan"} trace their registration through the forty-one. #{ref :the_preservationists, "Preservationist"} practice makes household registration the gate to a settlement's examinations, and a result held on a disputed line carries a provisional note: the holder sits the paper, is marked, takes the post and holds it subject to the item. #{ref :bao_qiuyan, "Bao Qiuyan"} keeps the intake bench on such a note, and the annual petitions asking the register to close the item are shelved in the bay behind her.

    The settlement's assembly has ruled twice that a provisional post carries full authority while the item stands. Both rulings were entered, and one of them was written by a clerk whose own line runs through the disputed forty-one.
  PROSE

  prose <<~PROSE, section: :tensions, heading: "The Offer From The Corridor"
    The #{ref :the_gatekeepers, "Gatekeepers"} have twice offered to settle it. They hold audited access to pre-2052 registration copies in network-held archives, they quote a fee against their published schedule, and they have reconciled worse discrepancies for other clients on the corridor.

    Juyan refused both offers in writing and shelved both refusals with the item. The reasoning entered on the line is that a return arriving out of the #{ref :the_great_root, "Great Root"}'s archives cannot be certified as the work of a human office, and a register the settlement cannot certify is not a register it can hold in trust. The Gatekeepers' standing reply, filed and also shelved, is that eleven households are paying the price of the distinction.
  PROSE
end
